  "details": "It would be nice to have dedicated inputs for controllers for features such:\n\n1. TextBox\n\n2. Face View\n\n3. 3rd Person View\n\nThere are current inputs such as:\n\n1. Start for menu\n\n2. Right Stick Press for action Wheel\n\n3. Y for mic\n\nThis was highlighted by the introduction of the new desktop UI that has parts of the UI showing controller inputs but just has bad formatting where no bindings are present. While I do not want to suggest any particular approach to solve this it would be nice to be able to provide the new accessibility from the labelled inputs to controller/ gamepad users as well.\n\nI also wanted to add that currently through the steam input system I was able to get all features in the Desktop UI to work by using the keyboard input bindings to the D-Pad. So even if you were not going to add native input at least displaying the bindings to the user would be great!\n\nTested on Xbox Controller\n\nCanny for formatting issues: https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1912-ui-formatting-starts-to-formatting-weird-with-controller",
